<% content_for :title, "My Omarchy" %>
<% content_for :no_my_nav, "1" %>
<div class="content-page container my-welcome">
  <p class="eyebrow">My Omarchy</p>
  <h1>Your Omarchy, on every machine.</h1>
  <p class="lede">One account for the things that should follow you around: your config, the
    screenshots you share, and dictation that works anywhere.</p>
  <div class="my-actions">
    <%= link_to "Sign in", new_session_path, class: "button" %>
    <%= link_to "How it works", my_setup_path, class: "button button--ghost" %>
  </div>

  <div class="my-features">
    <section class="my-feature">
      <h2>Dotfile sync</h2>
      <p>Push a snapshot of your Omarchy config from any machine, pull it on the next. Whole
        snapshots, kept for you, nothing merged behind your back. Encrypt them before they
        leave the machine if you like — we store what you send.</p>
      <pre>$ omarchy my sync push
$ omarchy my sync pull</pre>
    </section>
    <section class="my-feature">
      <h2>Share a snap</h2>
      <p>Hit share in <a href="https://github.com/omacom/omasnap">omasnap</a> and get a link on
        your clipboard. Unguessable, never listed, optional expiry, and a proper preview card
        wherever you paste it.</p>
      <pre>$ omarchy my snap share ~/Pictures/Screenshots/latest.png</pre>
    </section>
    <section class="my-feature">
      <h2>Voice, anywhere</h2>
      <p>Local dictation is great on a fast machine. On a laptop, hand transcription to the
        cloud: a personal, spend-capped key you can revoke any time, wired into voxtype in
        one command.</p>
      <pre>$ omarchy my voice setup</pre>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>
